{
  "description": "Packed audit disclosures of confidential ring transfers at capacity 2 and 4, one case per layout: none, exits, escrow, data_free and exits_escrow. Hex strings are big-endian, fields 32 bytes. Domain tags are ASCII as one field: CRBS, CROD, TXOB, TXOS. Fixed inputs: tx_viewing_sk is the clamped X25519 transaction secret and tx_viewing_u its public key, salt, first_nullifier n0, ring_id = hash_bytes(ring_program_id), blinding_seed = Poseidon(CRBS, pack_be(tx_viewing_sk), salt), seed_out = Poseidon(TXOS, n0, blinding_seed), output_tree_id. layout is the audit statement's flag value exits | key_escrow << 1 | data_free << 2 | full_openings << 3, read from the ring frame, the auditor takes the disclosure layout from that frame and the published output count. Per slot: owner_key is a raw Solana key whose owner identity is hash_bytes(0x53 || owner_key), nullifier_pk, asset = hash_bytes(asset_address), amount, data_hash, ring_data_hash, owner_tag is the published owner tag (the recipient u of a ring output, the owner key of an exit, random bytes on a dummy). Every slot has blinding = Poseidon(TXOB, n0, seed_out, i). output_hash is the SPP UTXO hash under output_tree_id, owner Poseidon(owner identity, nullifier_pk), ring id ring_id on a ring output and 0 on an exit, a dummy hashes under the dummy domain with zero fields. plaintext: seed_out first when an output exits, then per slot nullifier_pk unless key_escrow, asset, data_hash and ring_data_hash unless data_free, and pack_disclosure(owner_key || u64be(amount)), every field of a dummy zero. Under key_escrow the auditor takes each owner's nullifier_pk from its escrow record. pack_disclosure cuts bytes into 31-byte chunks, each behind one zero byte, the last chunk zero padded at its end. pad[j] = Poseidon(Poseidon(CROD, pack_be(tx_viewing_sk), salt), j), published[j] = (plaintext[j] + pad[j]) mod q, disclosure_chain = HashChain4(published). Generated by sdk-libs/client/tests/disclosure_vectors.rs.",
